[statement]
A sparse file in GNU's pax format 1.0 whose POSIX header ends in star's
trailer, `tar` and a NUL, with star's two times as star writes them,
eleven digits and a space. GNU tar lists the file and nothing after it.
bsdtar, Python and Go list the member after it too. ferrotape refuses the
archive.

[archive]
pax GNU.sparse.major=1 GNU.sparse.minor=0 GNU.sparse.name=sp GNU.sparse.realsize=2048
header name=GNUSparseFile.0/sp size=1024 @476="00000001750 00000003720 " @508="tar\0"
data "1\n1536\n512\n""\0"*501"S"*512
header name=tail
data "hello\n"
end

[verdict]
strict: refused Sparse(PaxForm) at 1024
compatible: refused Sparse(StarTrailer) at 1024

